---
const year = new Date().getFullYear();
---
<footer class="border-t border-ink-300/30 bg-paper-alt mt-12">
  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 py-8 text-sm text-ink-500 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-4">
    <div>
      <p class="text-ink-700 font-medium">FloodWatch.PH</p>
      <p>
        Open-source observed flood extent from public SAR satellite data. Sentinel-1 C-band, permanent-water-masked, event-disjoint validated. Track A: event flood extent. Track B: recurrence-prone classifier. Code MIT, data CC-BY-4.0. Not affiliated with PAGASA, NDRRMC, or UP NOAH.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="text-ink-700 font-medium">What this isn't</p>
      <p>
        An official hazard map or engineering assessment. Observed flood extent from satellite is not a substitute for a formal flood risk study. The civic finding is the gap between observed recurrent flooding and official hazard-map coverage. Language stays conservative: "observed extent" and "warrants verification," not allegations.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="text-ink-700 font-medium">Found an error?</p>
      <p>
        Open an issue or PR on <a href="https://github.com/xmpuspus/floodwatch-ph" class="no-underline text-ink-700 hover:text-ink-900">GitHub</a>. Especially welcome: verified flood extents not captured in our data, province boundary corrections, official hazard-map sources for the v1.1 overlay.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="text-ink-700 font-medium">Privacy &amp; takedown</p>
      <p>
        <a href="/privacy" class="no-underline text-ink-700 hover:text-ink-900">Privacy &amp; responsible use</a> &middot;
        <a href="/faq" class="no-underline text-ink-700 hover:text-ink-900">FAQ</a> &middot;
        <a href="https://github.com/xmpuspus/floodwatch-ph/issues/new?labels=takedown&amp;template=takedown.md" class="no-underline text-ink-700 hover:text-ink-900">request takedown</a>. DPO: xpuspus@gmail.com.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="md:col-span-4 text-xs text-ink-500 pt-4 border-t border-ink-300/20 leading-relaxed">
      <p class="mb-1">
        Observed flood extent derived from public satellite data (Copernicus Sentinel-1, Google AlphaEarth, Global Flood Database, MERIT Hydro, JRC Global Surface Water, WorldPop, Microsoft GlobalML Footprints, FAO GAUL level-2 boundaries). FloodWatch.PH computes statistical indicators only. Patterns may have legitimate explanations; figures warrant independent verification. All exposure figures are province-level aggregates (FAO GAUL level-2, ~82 Philippine provinces; city and barangay resolution is a v1.1 refinement). No household geometry, no per-dwelling flood status, no PII property keys.
      </p>
      <p>
        &copy; {year} FloodWatch.PH. Cite as: FloodWatch.PH ({year}), https://github.com/xmpuspus/floodwatch-ph. CC-BY-4.0 on data.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</footer>
